---
title: Cancellation and Refund — the client's published policy
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    participant W as Next.js
    participant A as NestJS API
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    participant S as Stripe
    participant M as Email

    C->>W: Cancel my booking
    W->>A: POST /bookings/:id/cancel
    activate A
    A->>D: Load booking, session, and the workshop's RefundPolicy
    A->>D: Load SA public holidays
    A->>A: Business days between now and session.startsAt

    alt More than 14 business days
        A-->>W: Offer a choice
        W-->>C: Full refund, or a credit voucher valid 6 months?
        alt Customer chooses refund
            C->>W: Refund to my card
            W->>A: confirm
            A->>S: Refund 100% of the amount stored on the booking
            Note right of A: Always the snapshotted amount,<br/>never the current price
            A->>D: Booking → REFUNDED, record refundedAmountCents
        else Customer chooses voucher
            C->>W: Give me a voucher
            W->>A: confirm
            A->>D: INSERT credit (kind VOUCHER, expires in 6 months)
            A->>D: Booking → CANCELLED
        end
    else 14 business days or less
        A->>A: Apply $15 per person late fee
        A->>D: INSERT credit for the balance after the fee
        A->>D: Booking → CANCELLED
        Note right of A: Open question — voucher or cash?<br/>Her policy implies voucher. Confirm.
    end

    rect rgb(232, 237, 244)
    Note over A,D: Whatever the outcome, the seat goes back
    A->>D: Release seats in the same locking transaction that took them
    end

    A->>M: Send cancellation confirmation
    A-->>W: outcome
    deactivate A
    W-->>C: Cancelled, with what you receive

    rect rgb(253, 246, 227)
    Note over C,M: The other three cases
    opt Customer does not turn up
        Note right of A: No refund, no voucher, no reschedule
    end
    opt Studio cancels the session
        A->>S: Full refund
        Note right of A: Or reschedule, or a gift card —<br/>the customer chooses
    end
    opt Admin overrides
        Note right of A: Rehana can always be generous.<br/>The policy is a default, not a lock.
    end
    end
